From: AX6 EDMA correctness audit
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] edma_v1: fix TX teardown consumer index double increment

edma_cleanup_txdesc_ring_res() executes two consecutive increments on
the consumer index:

    cons_idx = (cons_idx + 1) & mask;
    cons_idx++;

The first line increments modulo ring size (correct), but the second
line does an unconditional +1 that skips the next descriptor. This
leaves one descriptor per wrap unprocessed and its skb leaked.

Remove the duplicate increment. Also fix the wrap handling to avoid
index confusion when the ring wraps around.

Fixes F6 from AX6 cross-audit 2026-07-26.
⚠ PATCH NEEDS BUILD-TREE VERIFICATION: the exact teardown loop
  structure, variable names (cons_idx, mask), and wrap logic must
  be confirmed against QSDK source.

--- a/hal/dp_ops/edma_dp/edma_v1/edma_cfg.c
+++ b/hal/dp_ops/edma_dp/edma_v1/edma_cfg.c
@@ -XXX,XX +XXX,XX @@ static void edma_cleanup_txdesc_ring_res

 	for (i = 0; i < EDMA_TX_RING_SIZE; i++) {
 		/* ... skb cleanup per descriptor ... */

-		cons_idx = (cons_idx + 1) & mask;
-		cons_idx++;
+		cons_idx = (cons_idx + 1) & mask;

 		/*
 		 * Handle wrap: the hardware may have wrapped the
-		 * consumer index. Re-read the producer to stay in sync.
+		 * consumer index. Keep the modulo result; the next
+		 * iteration will advance correctly.
 		 */
-		if (cons_idx == 0)
-			cons_idx = edma_hw.txdesc_rings[ring].prod_idx & mask;
 	}

 	edma_hw.txdesc_rings[ring].cons_idx = cons_idx;
